	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Barrens is a vast savannah of yellow grass, thorn trees and cracked red earth in the heart of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. It stretches from the forests of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link} in the north to the canyons of {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link} in the south, and from the cliffs of {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon{/link} and {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} in the west to the shore of the Great Sea in the east. Few places in the world are so wide, so dry or so full of life that bites. Herds of kodo and zhevra cross it, lions and raptors hunt it, and a dozen peoples fight over its scattered water. Every road of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} runs through it, and every enemy of the Horde knows it.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The chroniclers of the tauren say that the Barrens was once a green and teeming land. War and cataclysm scorched it long ago and left a dry husk behind, and no one living remembers it otherwise. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} roamed its plains for generations, hunted from one camp to the next by the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}. The {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} raised their thorn warrens in the south, and the {link:harpies}harpies{/link} nested on its western hills.

When the orcs came to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} after the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} led them across these plains. On the long march he met {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} and his people under centaur attack, and the orcs guarded the tauren caravans until they reached {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}. After the war at {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link}, the {link:horde}Horde{/link} made the Barrens the road between its new homes: {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} and {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} to the east, {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} to the west.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[The Barrens belongs to the {link:horde}Horde{/link} in name, and to whoever is strongest in each valley in truth. {link:the-crossroads}The Crossroads{/link}, a fortified town of orcs, holds the center. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} of {link:camp-taurajo}Camp Taurajo{/link} guard the south. Goblins of the {link:steamwheedle-cartel}Steamwheedle Cartel{/link} trade with every side at the port of {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link}.

Enemies press in from every quarter. The {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar centaur{/link} have found new leaders. The {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane{/link} and {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback quilboar{/link} war on the Horde and on each other. Soldiers of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link} hold {link:northwatch-hold}Northwatch Hold{/link} on the coast, dwarves of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} dig at {link:bael-modan}Bael Modan{/link}, and the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} poisons a lake in the north. Cultists of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} work their rites on {link:dreadmist-peak}Dreadmist Peak{/link}. Strangest of all, the oases have begun to change, and the druids fear that something beneath the land is dreaming.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link}.{/b} Orc grunts, {link:tauren}tauren{/link} braves, troll scouts and a few {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} apothecaries keep the posts and roads.
• {b}The goblins of {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link}.{/b} Traders, tinkers and bruisers who sell to anyone who pays.
• {b}The {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}.{/b} The {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar tribe{/link} raids the oases and the roads.
• {b}The {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link}.{/b} The {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane{/link} hold the north and the southern ridges, the {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback{/link} the center.
• {b}The {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.{/b} The marines of {link:northwatch-hold}Northwatch Hold{/link} and the dwarves of {link:bael-modan}Bael Modan{/link}.
• {b}The {link:southsea-pirates}Southsea Freebooters{/link}.{/b} Pirates who have made camp on the {link:the-merchant-coast}Merchant Coast{/link}.
• {b}The beasts.{/b} Kodo, zhevra, plainstriders, savannah lions, sunscale raptors, thunder lizards and thunderhawks.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Dry Land.{/b} Long before the orcs came, the Barrens was burned and dried by war and cataclysm. No chronicle records when.
• {b}The Long March.{/b} {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s orcs crossed the plains, fought off the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} and brought {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link}'s tribes safely to {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}.
• {b}The {link:horde}Horde{/link}'s Road.{/b} After Hyjal, the orcs raised the {link:the-crossroads}Crossroads{/link} and the watchtowers of {link:gold-road}the Gold Road{/link}. The goblin {link:gazlowe}Gazlowe{/link} founded {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link} with the gold he earned building {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} New oases bubble up from the earth, and with them new and twisted creatures.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Plains",
			text = [=[• The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} give the great beasts of the Barrens names of their own: Echeyakee, Whitemist, is the king of the savannah cats, and {link:lakota-windsong}Lakota{/link}'mani, Earthshaker, is the greatest of the kodo.
• The sunscale raptors of the Barrens are cleverer than their kin in other lands. They once stole the silver meant to pay the guards of the {link:the-crossroads}Crossroads{/link}, and no one has yet explained why.
• A caged {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} at {link:camp-taurajo}Camp Taurajo{/link} still works the magic of Agamaggan. He sells it for revenge on the tribe that left him there.]=],
		},
	},
})

