			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Razormane are a tribe of {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} of the northern and southern {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}. They raise their camps among great thorn vines that grow up from the earth, and they revere the boar spirit Agamaggan, whose blood is said to have made the thorns. Before the orcs came, they roamed the land that is now {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}, and they have never accepted its loss.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In These Days",
			text = [=[The Razormane are at war with the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and with their cousins of the {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback{/link} tribe. They hold {link:thorn-hill}Thorn Hill{/link} east of the {link:the-crossroads}Crossroads{/link}, {link:bramblescar}Bramblescar{/link} in the middle plains and {link:blackthorn-ridge}Blackthorn Ridge{/link} in the south. Their raids on the caravans from {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} were led by three of their tribe who came out of {link:razorfen-kraul}Razorfen Kraul{/link}: {link:nak}Nak{/link}, Kuz and {link:lok-orcbane}Lok Orcbane{/link}. The smith of {link:camp-taurajo}Camp Taurajo{/link} has found that their weapons are growing sturdier. In a cave on Thorn Hill, the Razormane speak of a monstrous beast of their own blood, the Ravener.]=],
		},
	},
})
